-- module `ifdefs` — the INTERFACE-METHOD rename corpus for the rename gate
-- (`ifacemethod.jsonl`).  ⚠️ THE LINE NUMBERS BELOW ARE THE TRANSCRIPT'S CLICK
-- COORDINATES — keep this header exactly 11 lines.  This shape used to be the
-- F3(d) span-verification case: `refindex.mdk`'s `defsOfDecl` recorded an
-- interface's method declarations at the enclosing decl's name `Loc` — the
-- INTERFACE name — so the edit landed on `Shp` and produced source that no
-- longer parses; `renameEmitVerified` (lsp.mdk) refused it.  **#1013 fixed that
-- Loc**, so the transcript now asserts the POSITIVE outcome: the interface's own
-- method declaration, BOTH impl clause heads and both call sites, five edits, and
-- the applied module still checks.  The corpus's F3(d) negative case moved to
-- `pun.jsonl` (a record-update pun, whose element `Loc` the parser drops).
interface Shp a where
  zoneArea : a -> Int

data Sqr = Sqr Int

impl Shp Sqr where
  zoneArea (Sqr s) = s * s

data Rct = Rct Int Int

impl Shp Rct where
  zoneArea (Rct w h) = w * h

zoneTotal : Int
zoneTotal = zoneArea (Sqr 3) + zoneArea (Rct 2 5)
